    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "kurai \n\nliterally means how long or much, but often used in conversation for adding an \"about\" feeling to soften a phrase.\n\nsometimes pronounced gurai depending on the phrase before; for example if the sentence before ends with a vowel.\n\n3万ドルぐらい = about 30,000 dollars",
      "html": "kurai <br/><br/>literally means how long or much, but often used in conversation for adding an \"about\" feeling to soften a phrase.<br/><br/>sometimes pronounced gurai depending on the phrase before; for example if the sentence before ends with a vowel.<br/><br/>3万ドルぐらい = about 30,000 dollars",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "8896f7768f4e12557c892d0899e269f6ce90cf0247516588e10bfdc2ed4ca13b",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "can also mean \"if anything\", \"rather\"",
      "html": "can also mean \"if anything\", \"rather\"",
      "credits_raw": "KotatsuSama",
      "content_sha256": "447bacb652fdd3bc8cecb3818b448fe74eaf48eb927732a5767508124ed9d1f2",
